# Deploy is part of the job

Cloudflare Pages serves **https://1min.to** from GitHub `main` (`onemin-to`). Local file edits do **nothing** on the live site until they are on `main`.

## Required workflow for any live-facing change

Applies to money hops, quiz JS/CSS, paths under `public/`, `functions/`, redirects, cloaker exit URLs, copy on landers, etc.

1. Make the change in the repo.
2. **Commit** with a clear message.
3. **`git push origin main`** (or `git push -u origin HEAD` on `main`) in the same task — do not stop at “updated locally.”
4. **Verify live** with cache-bypass (`?_=timestamp`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`) on `https://1min.to/...` (and `r.html` / hop pages if relevant). Confirm the new URL/content is present.
5. Only then tell the user it is done / live.

## Do not

- Leave live URL or cloaker-exit changes uncommitted or unpushed.
- Say “done” when only the working tree changed.
- Assume Cloudflare has deployed instantly — poll until live HTML matches, or say push succeeded and deploy is still propagating if verification is still old after a short wait.

## Money URLs

Never commit offer/money destinations into `public/`. Only `functions/` (or `MONEY_URLS` env) may hold them. Public files may only reference `/api/go`.

## Exception

Skip push only if the user explicitly says not to push / deploy.
